{
  "outcome": "DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL",
  "best_model_id": "PGS002237",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "All 22 candidates are direct matches at the EFO level, but they vary in endpoint fidelity and in whether reported discrimination is PRS-comparable. PGS002237 is the most disease-focused direct CKD model in this set: it targets a clearly defined clinically meaningful endpoint (CKD stage 3+ with eGFR <45 ml/min/1.73m2), comes from a dedicated CKD PRS paper (\"Genome-wide polygenic score to predict chronic kidney disease across ancestries\", Nat Med), has large stated training (n=279,819, UKB) and multi-ancestry evaluation, and reports supportive effect size (OR=1.47) plus AUROC=0.78 in European validation. The main limitation is that the reported AUROC appears to be from a covariate-augmented/full model with many clinical risk-factor covariates (e.g., hypertension, diabetes, BMI, medication use), and no PRS-only AUROC/R2 is provided here, reducing cross-model comparability and making it unclear how much of the AUROC is attributable to the PRS itself. Several alternative direct-match candidates have cleaner/no covariates (e.g., the 2023 five-biobank family with covariates=0), but they show substantially lower full-model AUROCs (~0.59) and/or lack PRS-only metrics, so the evidence does not support a clearly high-quality single winner."
}

