  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates for COPD are present (e.g., PGS001332/PGS001333/PGS001334/PGS001783/PGS001788/PGS001850/PGS002062/PGS004466/PGS004536). Prioritizing endpoint fidelity, several are exact COPD/J44 matches; among those with PRS-comparable signal reported, PGS001783 provides a covariates-regressed-out Nagelkerke R2=0.038092 in EUR evaluation, which is consistent with the provided COPD heritability ceiling (h2_liability=0.0388), and it comes from a large multi-biobank development context (Cell Genom; many cohorts listed) rather than a single-biobank pan-trait/portability sweep. Competing exact-label snpnet UKB framework scores (PGS001332/PGS001333/PGS001334) show low PGS-only performance (PGS AUROC ~0.54; PGS R2 ~0.002–0.003) and appear largely covariate-driven (full-model AUROC ~0.72–0.73 with small incremental AUROC ~0.003–0.004), while the portability study models (PGS001850/PGS002062) lack standard AUC/R2 and only report partial-r, and the 2024 J44 models (PGS004466/PGS004536) report only an OR without comparable discrimination metrics and have unknown covariates. Confidence is not high because key metrics are missing or non-comparable for several contenders (notably the 2024 J44 scores), and PGS001783’s AUROC is not reported as PGS-only."
